Terrence, Camille,<br />
<br />
Working back through Marcus's index. The single October 2013 hit is the bet=
ter document and I nearly walked past it.<br />
<br />
On October 21, 2013 the same chief compliance officer wrote to Achterberg w=
ith no examination open, nobody asking, and no obligation to report anythin=
g. Marchwood had acquired the Hollis Grange book. She wrote that the 2011 u=
ndertaking "is not limited in time and by its terms reaches accounts we acq=
uire," and then described applying it: all 61 acquired accounts now at Sign=
al Peak, the 53 not already there moved on October 14, 2013, fourteen inher=
ited fee-debit authorizations revoked rather than assigned, clients re-pape=
red onto agreements without withdrawal authority, and Quillen and Marsh eng=
aged for the 2013 surprise examination.<br />
<br />
The motion's theory is that Marchwood was never told to do anything. Two ye=
ars after the examination closed, unprompted, Marchwood told us what it was=
 doing to comply with the thing it says it was never told to do, and did it=
 at its own cost on a book it had just bought.<br />
<br />
Delphine